From 9833c3f105af2f79bdfc0997cb4e7dfb2b870eea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:41:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0147: layout-aware HUD runtime matcher + restore to the
 .bflyt base

The name-only matcher moved capture CONTENT panes (TxtCounterSh /
TxtCounter / TxtIconSh / TxtIcon, shared by CounterCoin and
CounterCollectCoin), which emptied the 128x128 capture texture (R1,
log-51), and hit the wrong layouts ('Counter' was the moon tower,
'PicStrap' the BootLoading strip, R2). Only a layout's 'All' container
is matched now, identified by its direct children: PicMap (compass),
Life (lives), Shine -> TxtShine (moons), Add + Capture tx 0 / 130
(coins / regional; All tx nearest -740 / -615 is the fallback, and no
Capture sibling matches nothing). Restore on mask 1 -> 0 writes the
local back to e_orig and marks dirty so the game recomposes +0x70;
+0x70 itself is never restored to e_mod, and the entry is released
once restored and visible. Mask-0 elements take no entry and write
nothing. The 0118 auto-edge early return is gone (it skipped restore
on 16:9). 0142 absolute-global write kept; HUD_EDGE_SLOTS_PER_ELEM
stays 16. hud_edge.c, _hud_edge_frame_step, HUD_EDGE_WORDS and
HUD_PROBE_WORDS deleted from this profile; HUD_RUNTIME_WORDS
regenerated from .text only (764 words).
