-# hud_probe, compiled from hud_probe.c (hud_probe at +0) with the same
-# flags as hud_edge. A diagnostic-only stub (0129): it writes compact
-# binary records into a probe buffer in the frame-step state page (state +
-# 0x3300, after the hud_edge table) and changes nothing about the HUD -- no
-# pane is moved, no transform is applied, no slot is taken. The host
-# (hud_manual.c dm_hud_probe_tick, once per present) formats the records
-# into "[hudprobe] ..." log lines. It takes everything through its
-# arguments, so these words are position-independent and relocation-free:
-#   x0 = the pane, x1 = the aspect (state + 0x58), x2 = the table (state +
-#   0x300), x3 = the probe buffer (state + 0x3300).
-# What it logs (first sighting per pane address, 256 addresses; the host
-# flushes the 13-record buffer every present, so a 5-second stand-still
-# logs every pane): the pane's name, parent, size, origin, flags and
-# global matrix; the aspect and the edge exactly as hud_edge reads and
-# computes them (the direct test of the edge = 0 hypothesis -- V1.3.18's
-# icons sit exactly one edge (140) from where 0128 should have put them,
-# and log-35 ruled hiding out as the trigger); and, for every pane hud_edge
-# matched, the decision it actually took (element index, slot, tdx/tdy/tk,
-# hidden, the parent's table entry and whether it is a fresh sentinel, and
-# the translation actually in the pane matrix); and (0131) for every pane
-# hud_edge matched, a layout record: the pane's own local translation
-# (+0x30/+0x34), the parent's local translation, and the stored original's
-# translation (e_orig[3]/e_orig[7]) after hud_edge -- the evidence 0130
-# needs, because 0130 had zero effect on device (log-38 identical to
-# log-37); and (0133) for every pane hud_edge matched, a chain record
-# (type 4): the local translations (+0x30/+0x34) of the pane and each
-# ancestor up to the root (five levels as floats, plus the depth walked),
-# and a fields record (type 5): the pane's and its parent's local scales
-# (+0x48/+0x4c), sizes (+0x50/+0x54) and origins (+0x5b), and the pane's
-# live global translation (+0x70) as the probe sees it -- the fields that
-# could hold the (263,71) layout, which log-41 proved is in no +0x30 in
-# the chain (H3); and (0134) for every pane named TxtCounterSh,
-# TxtCounter, Capture02, Capture03 or RootPane -- the coin number's own
-# chain, matched or not -- five hex-dump records (type 6): the pane
-# struct's raw bytes 0x00-0xFF in 60-byte chunks, so the (263,71) layout
-# (confirmed by the V1.3.17 screenshot re-measurement) can be found by
-# grepping for 263.0 = 0x43838000, 123.0 = 0x42F60000 or
-# 71.0 = 0x428E0000 if it lives in a field the probe has not read yet.
-# A matched target pane now takes ten records, an unmatched target pane
-# six; the 13-record cap is unchanged, so a flush carries the aspect
-# record plus one matched target pane and the rest defer.
-# Gated by the environment
-# variable DM_HUD_PROBE=1 (the host sets the buffer's enabled flag from
-# it). Delete after use; never ship.
